# The ability is not a leaves-the-battlefield ability, so it does not look back (CR 603.10a; ruling: it does not trigger
# "on any other cards going to the graveyard at the same time"). Engineered Explosives, with one charge counter (sunburst, one
# color spent), destroys every nonland permanent of mana value 1 at once: Planar Void and Bot2's Llanowar Elves reach the
# graveyards together, and with the Void gone the Elves are not exiled. The Explosives, sacrificed as a cost while the Void was
# still there, is exiled by it; the mana value 0 Moxes are left alone (the control that the right permanents were destroyed).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Planar Void
Engineered Explosives
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
